501 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. Executive Summary Low-code and no-code \(LCNC\) development has moved from a departmental productivity shortcut to a core pillar of enterprise software strategy. Industry analysts now estimate that roughly 70 to 75 percent of new enterprise applications will be built using low-code or no-code technologies, with the global market value climbing well past the sixty-billion-dollar mark and continuing to expand at a compound annual growth rate above 25 percent. This shift is not incremental; it represents a structural change in who builds software, how quickly it is built, and what governance is required to keep it safe.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 449 0 R
/Next 523 0 R
>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<<
/Title (This report surveys the most significant trends shaping low-code application development, synthesizes current market data, and outlines the risks and strategic actions that technology leaders should consider)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 449 0 R
/Prev 523 0 R
>>
endobj
