504 0 obj
<<
/Title (However, platform leaders are cautioning that this convenience has limits. As generative components move from prototypes into mission-critical systems, teams are beginning to encounter the classic problems of large language models, namely hallucinated logic and non-deterministic behavior, in contexts where predictability is essential. This has sparked renewed investment in hybrid architectures that combine deterministic, rules-based logic with AI-generated components only where appropriate. 3.3 The Citizen Developer Movement Matures)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 450 0 R
/Prev 525 0 R
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Title (Non-IT employees are projected to make up roughly four out of every five low-code users by 2026, up sharply from around 60 percent just a few years earlier. Rather than being treated as a governance risk to be minimized, citizen development is increasingly being formalized: organizations are creating structured enablement programs, internal centers of excellence, and clear escalation paths so that citizen-built applications can graduate into IT-supported production systems when needed.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 451 0 R
/Next 526 0 R
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Title (formalize approval workflows, mandatory review gates, and usage monitoring specifically for AI-assisted low-code development, rather than treating it as a simple extension of existing citizen development policy. 3.5 Composable, Multi-Cloud Architectures Low-code platforms are increasingly expected to operate as one component within a broader composable enterprise architecture rather than as a walled garden. The vast majority of enterprises now run multi- cloud environments, and low-code vendors are responding with deeper API management, event-driven integration, and support for headless or embeddable components that can be dropped into existing digital ecosystems. This composability trend also supports industry cloud platforms, pre-configured vertical solutions that combine low-code tooling with industry-specific data models, which are expected to see rapid enterprise adoption through the remainder of 2026. 3.6 Vertical and Industry-Specific Platforms Rather than positioning themselves as general-purpose builders, a growing share of low-code vendors are targeting specific industries with pre-built data models, compliance templates, and workflow accelerators. Healthcare, financial services, insurance, and the public sector are the most active adopters, drawn by platforms that arrive with regulatory scaffolding already in place. This trend reduces implementation time further and lowers the compliance burden that would otherwise fall on citizen developers working in sensitive domains. 3.7 Platform Consolidation and Toolchain Rationalization)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 451 0 R
/Prev 527 0 R
>>
endobj
